# Intent: Train 3 verification path (docs/design/unit-verification-plan-2026-11-16.md). A bench build can call the unit's own tools over the USB cable: a line "@tool self.mood.get" or "@tool self.timer.set {"seconds":30}" runs that tool through the same table the host uses, and the answer comes back on the cable as one "@reply" line; "@list" lists the tools. It changes no saved address and stops no link. It needs the cable and nothing on the network can reach it. Off by default: a shipped image has no reader and no USB driver.
# Placement: unit (a bench path in the robot firmware, off in every shipped image)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/hal_mcp.cpp of the StackChan main component (MIT); the McpServer ParseMessage response sender of the xiaozhi base (MIT)
# Check after a flash: with the option on, "@list" answers the tool list and "@tool self.battery.get_status" answers percent and charging; with the option off the build has no maipai_serial_tools object.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_SERIAL_TOOLS (default n).
